# Commonly-used variables setup and launcher command line.
#

# On startup the launcher changes into the directory of its executable and
# uses it as the installation root. So a test that gets the launcher past
# its options first clones it into the root/ subdirectory of its working
# directory, which then becomes the installation root. Note that the clone
# registers the copy for cleanup.
#
# We make the copy the test program so that $* runs it the same way as the
# original, including through the test runner, if any.
#
# Note that we hard link the executable rather than copy it. While a copy is
# being written, a process that a parallel test forks inherits the open file
# until it executes its program, and running the copy in the meantime fails
# with "text file busy" (ETXTBSY). Where hard links aren't supported, ln
# falls back to copying.
#
launcher = [path] $0
test = [path] "root/$leaf($launcher)"

clone_launcher = [cmdline] mkdir root && ln $launcher root/

# On Windows the copy also needs the DLLs of the in-tree dependencies, if
# any (there are none in a static build). They are in the assembly directory
# next to the original executable, which its manifest names. When we test
# under Wine we symlink the directory since its entries are relative
# symlinks that a copy would break. Natively we copy it since with the
# symlink the copy fails to start with an incorrect side-by-side
# configuration.
#
if ($cxx.target.class == 'windows' && $directory_exists("$(launcher).dlls"))
{
  if ($build.host.class == 'windows')
    clone_launcher = [cmdline] $clone_launcher && cp -r "$(launcher).dlls" root/
  else
    clone_launcher = [cmdline] $clone_launcher && ln -s "$(launcher).dlls" root/
}

# Options that keep the launcher from reaching outside the installation
# root (see launcher.cli for each).
#
offline = --skip-remote --no-shortcuts --no-connect-protocol
